WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.300
Laser-vision throat surgery to end the zombie
apocalypse?

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.360
Believe it or not, that's not even the weirdest
way a fight between Superman and Black Adam

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.360
has ended.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:13.400
In the comics, Black Adam is not a sworn enemy
of Superman.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.730
Regardless of The Rock's desire to see these
powerhouses trade blows on the big screen,

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.480
they don't actually have an official rivalry
with one another in DC lore.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.060
Black Adam, originally known as Teth-Adam,
was called the Mighty Adam after the Wizard

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.730
Shazam bestowed on him the ability to say
"Shazam!" and gain all his power.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.880
Unfortunately, Black Adam abused this power,
using it for selfish gain and then for evil.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.410
Because of this, the Wizard imprisoned Black
Adam, vowing to wait for the right person

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.728
to come along and be his next champion.

00:00:41.728 --> 00:00:44.480
"I was a slave until I died.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.084
Then I was reborn a god."

00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:53.149
Centuries later, Billy Batson is chosen to
wield the power of Shazam.

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:57.350
Because of this, Black Adam returns, hoping
to kill the boy and claim his powers.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.510
In some versions, Black Adam also kills both
of Billy's parents, though, in the most recent

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.830
origin, he simply wants the full Shazam powerset
to himself.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:10.110
Thus, Black Adam is traditionally the archnemesis
of DC's Captain Marvel, the hero more commonly

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:15.040
known today as Shazam and not to be confused
with Marvel's Carol Danvers.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.650
Because of his ties to the magic side of the
DCU, Black Adam rarely engages with Superman,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.320
who is vulnerable to magic.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.990
Generally, Black Adam and Shazam are more
closely involved with the Justice Society

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:29.259
of America, and, as comic book readers and
moviegoers alike will know, Superman is a

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:33.000
part of the Justice League, a totally different
superhero team.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.549
As a result, they mostly stick to their own
corners of the DC Universe.

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:40.540
However, these two big hitters have still
crossed paths on occasion.

00:01:40.793 --> 00:01:46.350
Black Adam first battled Superman in issue
#58 of "All-New Collectors' Edition," a comic

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.750
series that often pitted DC characters who
might not normally fight against each other.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.210
During this period in comic book history,
Superman and the Justice League's stories

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.400
took place in a world called "Earth-One,"
while the Marvel Family and Black Adam existed

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.119
in a world called "Earth-S."

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.439
The "S" is surprisingly not for "Shazam."

00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:06.549
In this issue the first ever crossover between
the Man of Steel and Shazam's fallen champion

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:07.750
took place.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.330
It all unfolds after Black Adam uses a spell
to disguise himself as Captain Marvel and

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.430
begins destroying Metropolis while posing
as Earth's Mightiest Mortal.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:21.030
Superman tries to stop the fake Captain Marvel,
who then uses Red Sun Radiation, a weakness

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.209
of Superman's, to disarm and defeat the Man
of Steel.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:27.989
Eventually, the real Captain Marvel returns
to Earth-One, but Superman, believing that

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:32.380
his former ally has gone rogue, attacks and
nearly kills Captain Marvel.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.660
Seeing this take place, the Wizard Shazam
explains the situation to Superman, who apologizes

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.250
to Captain Marvel for the beatdown.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:43.980
Black Adam, at the behest of Martian sorcerer
and scientist Karmang the Evil, plans to merge

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.959
the two worlds together in what could have
proven to be a cataclysmic event.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:52.530
Thankfully, the duo of Superman and Captain
Marvel thwart Karmang's plan and send Black

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.066
Adam back to Earth-S together.

00:02:54.066 --> 00:02:55.280
All in a day's work!

00:02:55.979 --> 00:03:00.959
A few years later, Black Adam returned to
the main DC Universe of Earth-One in "DC Comics

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:04.930
Presents" #49, which hit shelves in September
1982.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:09.400
In this issue of the famed DC team-up series,
Black Adam comes to Earth-One and attempts

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.700
to conquer the world, liking his chances because
it's a world without Captain Marvel.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:18.460
He also hopes to defeat Superman again in
the process, but he knows it won't be a simple task.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.950
As such, Black Adam decides to hold Earth
One's Billy Batson hostage and use him to

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:26.153
keep Superman from thwarting another one of
his plots.

00:03:26.153 --> 00:03:29.913
"Now I kneel before no one."

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.400
Though Superman at first tries to talk Black
Adam down and handle things diplomatically,

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.459
the supervillain refuses to yield.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.410
Instead of listening to reason, he engages
in an exceedingly dangerous battle with the

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.410
Man of Steel.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:45.350
Like before, Black Adam begins to overpower
Superman due to the magical nature of his

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.750
abilities, but the Kryptonian has a trick
up his sleeve.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.049
Superman manages to rescue Billy from Adam's
grasp and uses him to bring the Billy Batson

00:03:53.049 --> 00:03:56.069
of Earth-S to Earth-One so he can join the
fight.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:04:00.140
After a big battle involving Superman, Captain
Marvel, and Black Adam, the supervillain is

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.351
finally defeated.

00:04:01.351 --> 00:04:01.960
How?

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.329
It's pretty simple, really: Earth-One's Billy
Batson tricks him into saying "Shazam!," stripping

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:08.880
him of his powers and returning him to human
form.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.280
Captain Marvel then uses the few brief seconds
afterward to knock out Teth-Adam and keep

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.790
him from transforming into Black Adam again.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:20.185
And with that, he says goodbye to Superman
and they return to their own world.

00:04:20.589 --> 00:04:24.830
In the years that followed the Man of Steel
and Black Adam's second bout, Earth-One and

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:29.920
Earth-S, along with numerous other worlds,
were merged into a single New Earth that featured

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.900
Superman, Captain Marvel, and all of their
respective foes.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.800
Black Adam was reformed into something of
an antihero and even joined Captain Marvel

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.039
in the ranks of the Justice Society of America
at one stage.

00:04:40.039 --> 00:04:43.850
This wouldn't last though, and Black Adam
eventually associated himself with the Secret

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:48.669
Society of Supervillains, seeing it as his
best shot at protecting his people in Kahndaq.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:55.270
In 2005's "Action Comics" #831, Superman once
again finds himself at odds with Black Adam,

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.419
who himself is trying to prevent Doctor Psycho
from killing people in Metropolis.

00:04:59.419 --> 00:05:03.509
Black Adam, annoyed that he's been associated
with Psycho's crimes, engages in a pretty

00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:05.380
lengthy battle with Superman.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:09.930
The two appear evenly matched here as they
duke it out across Metropolis, but when Black

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:14.810
Adam shows little regard for the innocent
civilians around him, Superman gets even angrier.

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:21.057
"Heroes don't kill people."

00:05:21.057 --> 00:05:22.720
"Well I do."

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.800
After nearly pummeling Black Adam into orbit,
Superman is forced to stop when Black Adam

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.180
turns his back on him, banking on the fact
that he's not only the Man of Steel but a

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.319
man of honor.

00:05:32.319 --> 00:05:33.930
It's a gamble that pays off.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.650
The fight comes to an end and the pair strike
a deal with Doctor Psycho: He will release

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:42.440
the citizens of Metropolis from his mind control
if Superman allows him to walk free.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.400
Reluctantly, Superman agrees, though only
after Black Adam assures him that Doctor Psycho

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.316
will be punished for his actions.

00:05:48.316 --> 00:05:52.695
This would be the last battle between Superman
and Black Adam in the mainstream continuity.

00:05:53.102 --> 00:05:57.650
After Superman and Black Adam's New Earth
tussle, various "Crisis" events took place

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:03.577
across the DC continuity, changing the powers,
origins, and even the personalities of numerous characters.

00:06:03.577 --> 00:06:08.509
In the New 52 continuity, Black Adam briefly
fought an evil version of Superman from another

00:06:08.509 --> 00:06:11.979
Earth named Ultraman during an event called
"Forever Evil."

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:15.849
This scrap doesn't end well for Black Adam,
with Ultraman crushing his jaw and leaving

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:18.389
him unable to speak the magic word "Shazam!"

00:06:18.389 --> 00:06:22.630
Though he eventually heals, he is left humiliated
by the resounding defeat.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:27.569
After the DC Rebirth rebrand, Black Adam encountered
the Man of Steel on several occasions, including

00:06:27.569 --> 00:06:32.610
briefly in the "Doomsday Clock" limited series
and in the "Endless Winter" crossover event,

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:36.810
where he swore revenge on Superman after the
hero stopped him from killing the Frost King.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:40.860
However, his frustration with Superman would
be short-lived, as the Man of Steel would

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:45.139
invite Black Adam to "turn over a new leaf"
and join the Justice League.

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:48.740
Hoping for some fresh perspectives, Superman
thinks that Black Adam joining the League

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.509
would be good for everyone involved.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:55.648
It's a bold move that pays dividends, as Black
Adam learns to once again be the Mighty Adam.

00:06:55.764 --> 00:07:00.450
Though Black Adam doesn't battle Superman
all that often in the mainstream DC Universe,

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:04.540
there are a few different alternate realities
in which these two powerhouses face off against

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:05.540
one another.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:10.810
In 2020's "DCeased: Hope At World's End,"
a zombie-like Anti-Life Virus begins infecting

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.419
people across the world.

00:07:12.419 --> 00:07:16.500
Hoping to contain the virus and its spread,
Black Adam begins using lethal force against

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.400
his own citizens in Kahndaq.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.259
Unfortunately for Adam, he gets infected by
the disease at the moment he goes to invoke

00:07:22.259 --> 00:07:25.750
the name of "Shazam!," making Black Adam one
of the undead.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.889
Naturally, Black Adam infects his entire nation
and leads them toward global domination.

00:07:29.889 --> 00:07:35.110
In response, the Justice League sends Superman,
Martian Manhunter, Green Lantern, and Cyborg

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.540
to stop Black Adam.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:40.940
While his horde of zombies manages to escape,
Superman and his team nearly defeat Black

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.220
Adam before he recognizes their tactics and
retreats himself.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.300
Eventually, Superman uses his heat vision
to sever Black Adam's vocal cords so he can

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.690
no longer use the magic word "Shazam!"

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:53.798
It's brutal, but necessary under the circumstances.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:59.090
Though Superman and Shazam rarely share screen
time in animation outside of shows like "Justice

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:03.639
League Unlimited" and "Young Justice," they
did share top-billing in a DC Animated Original

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:06.000
where they fought against Black Adam together.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.770
That film is "Superman/Shazam!: The Return
of Black Adam," which retells the story of

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.640
how Billy Batson first gained the powers of
Shazam.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:17.599
In it, Black Adam returns to Earth to find
the Wizard's new champion, and decides to

00:08:17.599 --> 00:08:19.270
take the power for himself.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.550
When Black Adam shows himself, Superman works
to stop him from killing young Billy, and

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:27.780
the two battle across the Metropolis skyline
until Billy gains his Captain Marvel powers

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:31.139
and helps the Man of Steel take down his nemesis
for good.

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:35.490
This short proves that while Superman and
Black Adam aren't traditional adversaries,

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.780
there's certainly an appetite to associate
them with one another inside DC.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:43.680
Outside of this short film, Black Adam and
his dog Anubis recently appeared in the final

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:49.510
post-credits scene of "DC League of Super-Pets,"
where they encountered Superman and his dog Krypto.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.460
"Your owner's a hero too?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:52.049
Anti-hero.

00:08:52.049 --> 00:08:57.250
It's basically exactly like a regular hero
except way cooler."

00:08:57.250 --> 00:09:02.070
Between that and the "Black Adam" movie, it
seems like DC is trying hard to ignite a rivalry

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.960
between these two on the big screen.

00:09:05.029 --> 00:09:09.890
In the epic cinematic trailer for the massively
multiplayer online game "DC Universe Online,"

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:13.460
the Justice League battles members of the
Secret Society of Supervillains.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:18.212
In a shocking turn of events, the Society
begins to overpower and kill members of the League.

00:09:18.212 --> 00:09:22.920
After hearing the cries of his teammates,
Superman arrives to fight the Society, easily

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.890
taking down supervillain after supervillain
in the process.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:29.910
One of them is Black Adam, who barely manages
to hold his own against the Man of Steel.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:34.450
The 2013 fighting game "Injustice: Gods Among
Us" features Black Adam as a member of the

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:39.529
evil Superman's global group Regime, which
has taken over the planet to "keep it safe."

00:09:39.529 --> 00:09:43.820
As a member of the Regime, Black Adam runs
various errands for Superman, at least until

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:47.519
a good Superman from another world arrives
and quickly defeats him.

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:51.899
In the sequel, "Injustice 2," Black Adam is
a major player, working alongside members

00:09:51.899 --> 00:09:56.800
of Superman's Regime and Batman's Insurgency
to stop Brainiac from destroying the planet.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.779
Elsewhere, the evil Superman tussled with
Black Adam in the pages of the companion comic

00:10:00.779 --> 00:10:04.660
book series to the "Injustice: Gods Among
Us" video game franchise, too.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:10.589
The DC Extended Universe started in 2013 with
Zack Snyder's "Man of Steel" and went on to

00:10:10.589 --> 00:10:13.360
have varying levels of success, depending
on the project.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:18.260
Henry Cavill made his debut as Superman in
that film and would reprise the role in 2016's

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:24.400
"Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice," 2017's
"Justice League," and, of course, 2021's "Zack

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:28.839
Snyder's Justice League," the director's cut
of the critically bashed team-up movie.

00:10:28.839 --> 00:10:33.600
By far Earth's strongest protector, Superman
has battled alien invaders, monsters, and

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.170
even gods from other realms, making him a
formidable opponent.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:41.740
As a founding member of the Justice League,
Superman works alongside the DC Extended Universe's

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:45.620
most impressive heroes, but none of them can
match him in terms of power.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:50.929
However, now that Black Adam is on the scene,
there's a being who can potentially do just that.

00:10:50.929 --> 00:10:56.459
"Your magic is weak."

00:10:56.459 --> 00:11:00.839
Superman, played once again by Henry Cavill,
appears at the end of "Black Adam" with hopes

00:11:00.839 --> 00:11:05.180
of talking to the titular antihero about his
presence in the DC Universe, and there's no

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.399
doubt that this thread will lead to some interesting
places.

00:11:08.399 --> 00:11:12.139
What is a little strange is that it seems
as though there are no plans for Black Adam

00:11:12.139 --> 00:11:15.519
to face his comic book nemesis, Billy Batson,
any time soon.

00:11:15.519 --> 00:11:19.800
With Superman making cameo appearances in
both "Shazam!" and "Black Adam," maybe the

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:23.934
Man of Steel will be the bridge that brings
these classic enemies together on the big screen.

00:11:23.934 --> 00:11:27.880
Whatever the future holds for the rivalry
between Black Adam and Superman, we're excited

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:32.168
to see what comes next and how these two powerhouses
will interact with each other.

